      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so looking at the preliminary data, it looks like the increase in larceny is most pronounced in the areas where the immigrant/minority population has spiked the most. i'm trying to figure out if i should focus more on the ethnicity variable itself when we present this to the underwriting committee, or if that's too risky from a compliance standpoint? like, is it statistically sound to treat race as a proxy for risk here?",
